WEBVTT

00:00.920 --> 00:07.592
As I stand in the wind on a hill by a port town,

00:00.920 --> 00:07.592
minatomachi oka no ue kaze wo uke

00:07.656 --> 00:14.683
mezurashii kurai atama wa karappo

00:07.656 --> 00:14.683
my head feels unusually empty.

00:15.268 --> 00:21.940
I was watching the town from the south side of the shore.

00:15.268 --> 00:21.940
haruka minami mukougishi de kono machi wo miteita

00:21.965 --> 00:28.179
And so I sunk my unsteady passion into the depths of the sea.

00:21.965 --> 00:28.179
guratsuita jounetsu wo umi ni shizumeta

00:29.073 --> 00:34.745
This surging power...

00:29.073 --> 00:34.745
tome donaku afureru chikara

00:29.073 --> 00:31.160
Black Jack

00:36.247 --> 00:42.502
It's something hidden in everyone, everywhere.

00:36.247 --> 00:42.502
sonnamono wa darenimo dokonimo hisonde iru mono

00:43.296 --> 00:48.258
Day after day, everyone tries their best.

00:43.296 --> 00:48.258
mainichi mainichi minna ganbaru

00:49.829 --> 00:57.184
But people get annoyed when I mention it.

00:49.829 --> 00:57.184
sore wo ieba hito wa mina kemutagaru

00:57.685 --> 00:59.376
Oh FREEDOM

00:59.376 --> 01:01.369
will be there

01:01.389 --> 01:04.349
It makes me glad...

01:01.389 --> 01:04.349
yokatta

01:04.594 --> 01:12.074
That I found my place here.

01:04.594 --> 01:12.074
ibasho ga koko ni attakara

01:12.127 --> 01:13.645
Oh WISDOM

01:13.645 --> 01:15.494
will be there

01:15.522 --> 01:18.163
I searched for the reason

01:15.522 --> 01:18.163
sagashita

01:18.164 --> 01:25.212
why we can believe in the same air

01:18.164 --> 01:25.212
onaji kuuki shinjirarerukoto

01:25.797 --> 01:32.677
as long as we're alive.

01:25.797 --> 01:32.677
ínochi aru kagiri

01:32.678 --> 01:34.763
He weaves the thread of life with his miraculous control of a scalpel.

01:34.847 --> 01:37.031
The genius surgeon who lives on a cape.

01:37.183 --> 01:39.794
His name is Black Jack.

01:57.257 --> 01:59.903
This is so amazing!

02:00.183 --> 02:03.544
Hey Doc, there's a water buffalo.

02:04.688 --> 02:07.940
Sheesh. How can you manage to sleep?

02:07.941 --> 02:11.235
Pinoco-chan, we'll be at my dad's excavation site soon.

02:11.236 --> 02:11.986
Really?

02:11.987 --> 02:13.904
So be ready to get off.

02:13.905 --> 02:16.573
Archeology is fine and all,

02:16.574 --> 02:22.712
but how dare he call himself a father after leaving
behind his adorable children just to dig up junk.

02:23.123 --> 02:28.085
But his findings may become world-renowned!

02:28.373 --> 02:31.547
What if the ancient civilizations were
actually cultivated by aliens?

02:31.548 --> 02:35.801
When I imagine him discovering evidence
proving such a theory, I get so excited!

02:35.802 --> 02:38.429
A big snake!

02:38.471 --> 02:39.418
Snake?!

02:49.222 --> 02:52.311
Originally "A Challenge from an Unknown Being” by Tezuka Osamu

02:49.222 --> 02:52.311
A Challenge from an Unknown Being

03:08.272 --> 03:09.501
Dad!

03:11.629 --> 03:13.047
Dad!

03:14.632 --> 03:17.426
You've grown so much, Sharaku!

03:17.671 --> 03:21.430
Oh gosh. You're having all the fun.

03:22.432 --> 03:23.766
You brought Pogo?

03:23.950 --> 03:27.728
You were the one that gave her to
me, so I always keep her with me!

03:27.729 --> 03:29.039
Oh yeah?

03:29.303 --> 03:30.481
Hey Dad.

03:33.943 --> 03:36.236
You're so pretty.

03:36.777 --> 03:37.777
Oh, come on!

03:37.822 --> 03:38.947
Oh, sorry!

03:39.741 --> 03:41.533
You've gotten strong too.

03:42.223 --> 03:43.676
Oh, please.

03:45.705 --> 03:47.623
Welcome.

03:47.624 --> 03:49.500
So you must be Pinoco-chan.

03:49.530 --> 03:50.770
Nice to meet you.

03:50.794 --> 03:52.503
Thank you for the introduction.

03:53.004 --> 03:55.673
Dr. Black Jack, I'm Kenmochi.

03:55.674 --> 03:57.049
I really appreciate you...

03:57.050 --> 03:58.467
Watching after us.

03:58.468 --> 04:02.012
And I am truly grateful to you for saving my son's life.

04:02.013 --> 04:03.675
Thank you so much.

04:04.623 --> 04:07.037
It was Sharaku-kun who got himself through it.

04:07.315 --> 04:10.985
Dad, I can help with the excavation, can't I?

04:10.986 --> 04:12.486
Yeah. Help me!

04:12.571 --> 04:16.073
Maybe we can find something that'll
turn the world upside down.

04:16.122 --> 04:17.122
Really?

04:17.662 --> 04:18.662
Let's hurry!

04:19.327 --> 04:21.104
Sharaku! Me too!

04:21.208 --> 04:22.575
Let me try too.

04:22.628 --> 04:23.289
Sure.

04:23.435 --> 04:24.227
Yay!

04:25.459 --> 04:27.168
Oh, I already found something.

04:27.256 --> 04:28.256
What is it?!

04:28.983 --> 04:30.318
Ta-da!

04:30.376 --> 04:31.232
That's a snake!

04:31.256 --> 04:34.633
It's a tiny one.

04:32.803 --> 04:33.663
No!

04:43.351 --> 04:45.686
This mural is very mysterious.

04:45.769 --> 04:46.330
Mysterious?

04:46.483 --> 04:52.568
Normally, the pictures are about tribal myths or royalty.

04:52.569 --> 04:53.725
But this is...

04:54.821 --> 04:55.821
That's not what it's about?

04:56.190 --> 04:58.981
Some say it's a prophecy.

04:59.284 --> 05:01.842
A prophecy?

05:02.420 --> 05:05.483
Right. A drawing of something
that will happen in the future.

05:05.791 --> 05:11.680
We can find objects in it that can be interpreted
to be modern airplanes or flying saucers.

05:12.195 --> 05:13.920
Mysterious indeed.

05:14.383 --> 05:19.109
The more mysteries there are, the more areas
there are for archaeologists to study.

05:19.721 --> 05:22.848
There is something else just as mysterious though.

05:24.976 --> 05:29.480
Originally, I was only going to invite my children.

05:29.481 --> 05:35.403
But for some reason, I felt like I had to invite you too.

05:35.633 --> 05:40.728
It's as if someone was compelling me.

05:48.083 --> 05:51.985
Where did Sharaku go in the middle of the night?

06:25.589 --> 06:26.337
Sharaku...

06:26.580 --> 06:28.456
He's doing stuff in his sleep again.

06:38.008 --> 06:42.094
Abdol damral omnis nomnis belues horimak.

06:52.119 --> 06:54.899
Sharaku! Come back!

06:57.861 --> 06:59.670
Sharaku!

07:07.820 --> 07:09.288
Sharaku!

07:15.587 --> 07:17.004
Sharaku!

07:17.172 --> 07:18.827
Sharaku!

07:29.226 --> 07:30.226
Sharaku!

07:30.519 --> 07:32.728
What are you doing over there?!

07:33.647 --> 07:34.605
Go back.

07:35.148 --> 07:37.004
You're not wanted here.

07:38.026 --> 07:39.235
"Omae"?

07:38.026 --> 07:39.212
"Omae" is a cocky, arrogant style of addressing "you."

07:39.236 --> 07:40.626
Who do you think you're talking to?!

07:40.904 --> 07:43.114
He sounds like a different person...

07:46.284 --> 07:47.364
Sharaku!

07:50.455 --> 07:52.123
Something's coming.

07:52.124 --> 07:54.417
I'll protect you if it's a snake, Pinoco-chan.

08:00.799 --> 08:02.216
Doc!

08:02.217 --> 08:04.343
Don't wander around at night.

08:04.344 --> 08:07.054
You never know what you'll come
across at night in the jungle.

08:07.431 --> 08:09.807
But Sharaku...

08:22.279 --> 08:26.148
I've been expecting you, Dr. Black Jack.

08:26.324 --> 08:27.435
Who are you?

08:28.006 --> 08:31.782
A man that has been chosen to be the gatekeeper.

08:32.226 --> 08:37.461
It seems I was the only one who could
pick up their waves in the vicinity.

08:38.462 --> 08:39.377
Their?

08:40.380 --> 08:41.277
Come inside.

08:44.051 --> 08:45.687
We need to bring Sharaku back.

09:02.277 --> 09:03.562
Where did you take Sharaku?

09:03.779 --> 09:09.617
Both the boy and the doctor were
called here for a purpose.

09:09.618 --> 09:10.284
A purpose?

09:10.702 --> 09:12.020
One of ours is injured.

09:12.287 --> 09:15.022
We called you, Doctor, to help.

09:15.749 --> 09:18.501
I wasn't called here by anyone.

09:18.502 --> 09:21.195
They do not use telephones or letters.

09:21.463 --> 09:22.938
Instead, they manipulate minds.

09:23.395 --> 09:28.928
<i>It's as if someone was compelling me.</i>

09:31.348 --> 09:35.601
We thought we'd need the best doctor in this world.

09:35.602 --> 09:37.311
Please forgive us.

09:37.312 --> 09:39.105
And you turned Sharaku into a puppet!

09:39.106 --> 09:40.523
Give me my brother back!

09:41.024 --> 09:43.171
Please see our injured one first.

09:48.865 --> 09:51.367
Hey! Where is Sharaku?!

09:51.910 --> 09:55.067
No, this is the first time I've met him.

09:55.372 --> 09:57.542
I just know of his reputation.

09:59.626 --> 10:02.635
It's... No, no need to be afraid.

10:02.796 --> 10:07.325
He's not talking to you, Wato-san.

10:07.718 --> 10:09.411
Then to who?

10:09.720 --> 10:11.338
There's nobody else here.

10:14.307 --> 10:17.796
They said they want you to display your skills first.

10:18.562 --> 10:24.410
They want you to use my body to prove
that you're the best in this world.

10:24.985 --> 10:27.340
Operate on me.

10:28.300 --> 10:29.556
That's absurd.

10:29.865 --> 10:33.367
No doctor would ever use a scalpel
on a healthy man's body.

10:33.368 --> 10:34.424
Let's go back, Pinoco.

10:45.547 --> 10:47.381
Hey! What happened?!

10:47.382 --> 10:49.710
Quickly. Take care of me.

10:50.135 --> 10:53.345
Show them your skills.

10:53.346 --> 10:55.931
All my medicine and tools are back at my cottage.

11:00.771 --> 11:01.806
Sharaku!

11:02.407 --> 11:04.268
Use these, Doctor.

11:06.318 --> 11:07.777
My bag...

11:08.403 --> 11:09.857
You took it?

11:12.074 --> 11:14.326
The patient's in pain.

11:14.451 --> 11:15.534
Do you really have time for this?

11:17.037 --> 11:18.178
This is terrible.

11:18.413 --> 11:19.997
Some of his internal organs have ruptured.

11:19.998 --> 11:22.333
And severe burns too.

11:22.334 --> 11:24.627
Pinoco, did you see that aloe growing outside?

11:24.628 --> 11:26.587
Cut as much as you can and bring it here.

11:26.588 --> 11:27.463
OK.

11:27.464 --> 11:30.549
We'll use it to treat his burns.

11:30.675 --> 11:32.343
Aye-aye!

11:32.344 --> 11:34.670
Wato-san, find some clean water.

11:34.888 --> 11:36.013
Water?

11:36.014 --> 11:37.633
There's rainwater...

11:38.767 --> 11:40.476
There's water over there.

11:42.062 --> 11:43.104
"Go get it"?!

11:43.105 --> 11:44.875
How dare you talk to me like that?!

11:49.111 --> 11:50.122
A fountain?

11:51.154 --> 11:52.530
Hurry up.

12:10.000 --> 12:11.882
You really are a great doctor.

12:11.883 --> 12:14.343
The pain is already letting up.

12:14.746 --> 12:16.971
I only administered some spinal anesthesia.

12:16.972 --> 12:18.472
You're still bleeding.

12:18.473 --> 12:19.462
Don't move yet.

12:33.906 --> 12:35.399
<i>They're shards of something.</i>

12:54.804 --> 12:56.552
Who did this?!

12:56.610 --> 12:57.655
Show yourselves!

12:57.679 --> 13:00.306
It's unforgivable to hurt someone just so you can test me!

13:25.999 --> 13:28.250
We were attacked without warning.

13:28.251 --> 13:30.336
What are you talking about?

13:30.337 --> 13:31.119
Come this way.

13:52.192 --> 13:53.192
That's...

13:53.193 --> 13:56.112
Ohmigewdness!

13:56.488 --> 14:01.075
We are intelligent beings from another solar system.

14:01.443 --> 14:02.410
I get it...

14:02.411 --> 14:06.038
The aliens have taken over Sharaku's body...

14:07.082 --> 14:12.240
We're sending signals to this boy's brain
and controlling him through hypnosis.

14:12.671 --> 14:14.463
Why?!

14:14.757 --> 14:21.400
We chose this boy to be our interpreter
since his brainwaves are closest to ours.

14:23.640 --> 14:29.270
You have the technology to come all the way to
Earth and yet you can't even treat an injury?

14:30.230 --> 14:34.951
Our medical equipment was destroyed
in the attacks of the humans.

14:35.485 --> 14:38.237
It will take at least seven days of
this planet's time to repair them.

14:38.947 --> 14:41.824
But they won't survive that long,

14:42.210 --> 14:44.300
We had no other choice.

14:44.998 --> 14:50.450
We hate to rely upon the barbaric and primitive
method of surgery we just witnessed,

14:50.792 --> 14:54.368
but I desire to save their lives more.

14:55.057 --> 14:59.007
This barbarian doesn't know the anatomy of you guys.

14:59.384 --> 15:00.718
I can't operate on you.

15:00.903 --> 15:07.368
The vertebrates of this planet have
basically an identical system.

15:07.934 --> 15:09.977
Sorry, but I refuse.

15:10.237 --> 15:11.189
Why?

15:21.990 --> 15:24.825
Change my brother back to normal!

15:26.248 --> 15:28.245
Why do you refuse?

15:28.246 --> 15:31.123
Doc! Doc!

15:31.124 --> 15:34.543
I will not handle a patient I'm not confident I can cure.

15:34.709 --> 15:36.754
So you'd just let them die instead?

15:36.755 --> 15:39.314
Then we'll pay this planet back...

15:40.092 --> 15:43.010
the planet who attacked us even though we did not resist.

15:44.012 --> 15:49.376
You attacked us unilaterally, and now
you refuse to save our injured.

15:49.851 --> 15:52.353
We are willing to annihilate such a race in an instant.

15:54.815 --> 15:58.222
I will not practice while being threatened.

15:58.735 --> 16:04.557
And I have no interest in creatures who call doctors
primitive and rely only on machines.

16:05.117 --> 16:08.192
Doc, you're not going to help them?

16:08.610 --> 16:09.597
No.

16:09.897 --> 16:11.372
But what about the world?

16:11.373 --> 16:12.485
And Sharaku?

16:12.874 --> 16:15.584
They can contact NASA's medical team.

16:15.585 --> 16:17.405
They'll be happy to help them.

16:17.878 --> 16:19.046
I'm leaving.

16:20.324 --> 16:21.891
You won't help us?

16:22.217 --> 16:24.343
You're not going to hear our plea?

16:25.637 --> 16:27.221
Please help us!

16:29.141 --> 16:31.475
Please save my wife!

16:32.134 --> 16:32.931
Your wife?

16:33.603 --> 16:35.896
She is priceless to me.

16:36.440 --> 16:37.606
Please save her!

16:37.607 --> 16:39.984
Please save my wife!

16:39.985 --> 16:41.527
She is very important to me.

16:41.528 --> 16:43.863
Please save my dear wife.

16:43.864 --> 16:45.281
My wife...

16:45.412 --> 16:46.025
Please...

16:55.208 --> 16:57.048
It will cost you $2,000,000.

16:57.335 --> 16:58.953
Can you pay?

17:00.462 --> 17:01.274
Cost?

17:01.298 --> 17:03.322
I'm a doctor.

17:03.717 --> 17:07.073
I'm in an occupation where I get paid for
providing medical services to patients.

17:07.471 --> 17:11.452
Are you telling me you have no concept
of currency on your planet?

17:12.014 --> 17:16.593
Oh, you must mean the keraman, a primitive tool of trade.

17:17.105 --> 17:23.444
On our planet, things have progressed to where
gratitude is the only compensation given.

17:23.843 --> 17:27.708
On this primitive planet, you need this for everything.

17:28.330 --> 17:31.329
If you don't like it, go to a planet where
things have progressed more.

17:40.243 --> 17:41.243
Let me try.

17:44.049 --> 17:46.553
Wato-san, bring me some more water.

17:46.843 --> 17:48.135
Of course.

17:49.388 --> 17:51.222
So you're going to save her?

17:51.451 --> 17:53.474
Pinoco, be my assistant.

17:54.351 --> 17:55.976
Aye-aye!

18:01.050 --> 18:02.900
It's the real thing.

18:02.901 --> 18:04.276
So cool...

18:05.153 --> 18:09.858
<i>I see that the heart and lungs seem
to be quite similar to a human's.</i>

18:10.469 --> 18:13.510
<i>I could check better if we had an x-ray...</i>

18:15.038 --> 18:16.958
<i>She has the same injuries as that priest.</i>

18:17.249 --> 18:18.248
<i>I get it!</i>

18:18.417 --> 18:20.710
<i>He served as the x-ray!</i>

18:21.211 --> 18:25.005
<i>They must have copied her injuries exactly to his body.</i>

18:25.674 --> 18:27.133
<i>Now I see.</i>

18:27.134 --> 18:29.997
<i>I just need to perform an identical operation.</i>

18:38.812 --> 18:39.529
<i>What's this?</i>

18:39.855 --> 18:41.622
<i>A human has no such organ.</i>

18:42.023 --> 18:43.274
<i>How should I deal with this?</i>

18:43.900 --> 18:46.360
<i>Please save my wife.</i>

18:46.987 --> 18:49.184
<i>I see. It's a baby.</i>

18:58.749 --> 19:00.207
The operation is complete.

19:05.672 --> 19:07.298
Be glad, sir.

19:07.299 --> 19:09.657
Both the mother and child are safe.

19:25.317 --> 19:29.403
I'd like to give you this as a token of my esteem and love.

19:46.463 --> 19:47.630
<i>Mom...</i>

19:53.345 --> 19:55.554
<i>I accept your token.</i>

20:04.648 --> 20:05.314
A dream?

20:05.357 --> 20:08.442
I had a really nice dream.

20:08.443 --> 20:10.986
Huh? Where am I?

20:11.074 --> 20:14.146
Sharaku! Thank goodness!

20:14.533 --> 20:16.450
What? What's the matter?

20:17.160 --> 20:20.538
Doc, was it all a dream?

20:31.174 --> 20:33.070
Sharaku! Wato!

20:36.430 --> 20:37.996
There you are!

20:38.779 --> 20:40.289
I'm sorry, Dad.

20:40.343 --> 20:41.149
I'm sorry.

20:42.030 --> 20:43.454
I'm glad you're safe.

20:43.786 --> 20:45.533
Let's go, back to the campsite.

20:45.807 --> 20:47.180
We have breakfast ready.

20:48.120 --> 20:50.417
Must be nice to have a dad...

20:51.945 --> 20:53.404
What's all that money?

20:53.905 --> 20:55.114
It's...

20:57.159 --> 20:59.702
Let's not tell him.

20:59.703 --> 21:01.704
What are you talking about?

21:01.935 --> 21:04.165
It's a secret.

21:04.867 --> 21:05.544
Tell me!

21:05.834 --> 21:06.834
No way!

21:06.918 --> 21:07.960
Wait!

21:07.961 --> 21:09.346
Wait up, Sharaku!

21:12.758 --> 21:15.551
Is this... play money?

21:15.568 --> 21:16.154
Huh?

21:16.178 --> 21:19.714
They all have the same numbers.

21:19.973 --> 21:23.976
Those clay dolls must have copied
the one he showed them.

21:25.896 --> 21:30.066
So you worked for free again.

21:30.692 --> 21:33.760
No, I got their payment.

21:34.404 --> 21:35.529
In here.

21:36.323 --> 21:37.196
Huh?

22:10.497 --> 22:17.503
I want to capture your heart with my silly smile.

22:10.497 --> 22:17.503
itazura no hohemi de muchuu ni sasetaino

22:17.504 --> 22:24.676
Only look straight at me.

22:17.504 --> 22:24.676
massugu na kimi no me ni watashi wo utsushitene

22:24.721 --> 22:31.978
Being kind isn't good enough.

22:24.721 --> 22:31.978
yasashii dake dewa nanika tarinaino

22:31.979 --> 22:42.488
I want to get in touch with your true heart, deep
within the you that nobody else sees.

22:31.979 --> 22:42.488
dare nimo misenai kokoro no oku no sotto furetai

22:42.489 --> 22:47.869
Being in the gentle sunlight,

22:42.489 --> 22:47.869
yawaraka na hizashi abite

22:47.870 --> 22:57.253
I wish on the clover that plays the melody of dreams,

22:47.870 --> 22:53.075
yume wo kanaderu clover

22:53.530 --> 22:57.254
kaze ni negai wo nosete

22:57.254 --> 23:08.014
and I search for a ray of hope beyond the blue skies,

22:57.254 --> 23:08.014
aoi sora no mukou e kibou no hikari sagasuno

23:08.015 --> 23:13.102
because I want to stay by your side forever.

23:08.015 --> 23:13.102
zutto soba ni itakara

23:13.103 --> 23:26.073
The promise we made long ago in a far away place...

23:13.103 --> 23:26.073
haruka kanata de zutto mae kara

23:26.074 --> 23:32.997
is finally coming to a realization, overcoming the incredible distance,

23:26.074 --> 23:32.997
hikari ni terasare michibikareru youni

23:32.998 --> 23:43.883
just as it was lead by the light.

23:32.998 --> 23:36.931
sora no hate tooku

23:37.024 --> 23:43.824
toki wo koete ima tadori tsuku

23:45.050 --> 24:14.874
The War Continues

23:45.090 --> 23:45.924
You stay home.

23:46.024 --> 23:48.271
I'm not giving you the tickets.

23:48.717 --> 23:50.130
Will Lunan make it?

23:50.197 --> 23:52.064
This war needs to stop soon.

23:52.104 --> 23:53.936
You're against the war too?

23:54.744 --> 23:55.957
You don't want to get better?!

23:56.077 --> 23:58.687
Then they'll send him to the battlefield
as soon as he's better?!

23:58.760 --> 23:59.600
He is my son.

23:59.627 --> 24:01.434
Then treat him like one!

24:01.760 --> 24:03.103
Doctor, please take this.

24:03.284 --> 24:05.138
That doll better be all you're
getting from him.

24:05.284 --> 24:05.937
How do you know?

24:06.044 --> 24:07.581
Ever since then...

24:07.724 --> 24:08.724
I knew it.

24:08.924 --> 24:11.124
What is your mother like, Doctor?

24:11.599 --> 24:14.412
Next Karte - The War Continues.

24:16.086 --> 24:17.736
Karte NG...

24:18.976 --> 24:20.005
Sharaku!

24:20.132 --> 24:20.923
Sharaku!

24:23.174 --> 24:24.481
Pinoco-chan!
